# ============================================================
# .assetsignore — files EXCLUDED from Cloudflare Pages uploads.
#
# The Pages build output is the repo root (wrangler.toml:
# pages_build_output_dir = "."), which meant the ENTIRE repo was
# deployed as publicly downloadable static assets: internal notes
# (SESSION_NOTES.md, DEPLOYMENT.md …), the legacy FastAPI backend
# (backend/server.py), automation scripts with their topic history,
# test reports and CI config. Classic information disclosure —
# exactly what an attacker enumerating a static site looks for.
#
# Everything below stays in the repo (CI/dev still use it) but is
# never uploaded to Cloudflare. Gitignore syntax, relative to root.
#
# NOTE: functions/ must NOT be listed — Cloudflare compiles it into
# Pages Functions separately.
# ============================================================

# --- Internal documentation / notes (never public) ---
*.md

# --- Legacy backend + preview-only frontend source ---
/backend/
/frontend/

# --- Build & automation scripts, tests, reports ---
/scripts/
/tests/
/test_reports/

# --- Internal metadata & planning files ---
/design_guidelines.json
/gsc-priority-urls.txt
/gsc-url-list.txt
/memory/
/data/

# --- Repo/CI tooling config (not site content) ---
/.github/
/.emergent/
/.gitconfig
/.gitignore
/.deploy-trigger
/wrangler.toml
/package.json
/pytest.ini

# --- Backup / scratch files anywhere in the tree ---
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.log
*.csv
